## acm-kubectl (stdio, local)

Multicluster kubectl operations via local kubeconfig.

**Source:** [stolostron/acm-mcp-server](https://github.com/stolostron/acm-mcp-server) (Node.js, legacy clone at `acm-kubectl-server/`)
**MCP Server Name:** `acm-kubectl`
**Transport:** stdio (local Node.js process)

**Tools:**
- `clusters` -- List all managed clusters with status and endpoints
- `kubectl` -- Run kubectl commands on hub or any managed cluster
- `connect_cluster` -- Generate kubeconfig + RBAC for a managed cluster

Uses `KUBECONFIG` env var. No deployment needed -- runs locally. Works as long as the kubeconfig is valid.

**Rebuild after upstream changes:**
```bash
cd ~/Documents/work/ai/tools/mcp/acm-kubectl-server && git pull
cd servers/multicluster-kubectl && npm install && npm run build
```

